[E0437] Error: cannot return a `Part` that borrows `values`
    ╭─[ err/503_c_structs_answered_wrongly/main.wip:21:12 ]
    │
 20 │     val values: [i32; 2] = [1, 2]
    │         ───┬──
    │            ╰──── `values` declared here
 21 │     return Part(values: &values, count: 2)
    │            ───────────────┬───────────────
    │                           ╰───────────────── `values` is a local of `ofLocal`, dropped when it returns
    │
    │ Help: keep what it points at where the struct is used, and build the struct there
    │
    │ Note: a C struct that leaves a function may only point at what its reference parameters refer to
────╯
